GAL22V10
UA6R001E

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  base latch -> (0,0,1)  [SCHEMATIC-CORRECTED]
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; ua6_hd + drive DB15 (p18) AND DB14 (p19) LOW during reset.
; DB13 (p20) + DB12 (p21) Hi-Z.  /_DRVEN unchanged (working HD).
;
; ** SCHEMATIC CORRECTION 2026-08-01 (user, by continuity): UA4.16 (o16)
;    is /_CFGD15 -> DB15, NOT /_CFGD12/DB12 as the KiCad net labelled it.
;    So o16 is reached via DB15 = UA6 pin 18, not DB12/UA6 pin 21. **
;
; Target base latch (o16,o17,o18) = (0,0,1) arms UA4 /GALCLK1 line35 ONLY
; = the 2M $200000 window (verified). Corrected pin map (o17/o18 proven
; in-circuit; o16 corrected here):
;   o16 (UA4.16) <- DB15 (UA6.18)   -> drive LOW to force o16=0
;   o17 (UA4.17) <- DB14 (UA6.19)   -> drive LOW to force o17=0  [worked]
;   o18 (UA4.18) <- DB13 (UA6.20)   -> leave Hi-Z, natural 1     [worked]
;
; ua6_hd_b001 wrongly drove DB12 (p21) for o16 -> o16 stayed 1 -> base
; (1,0,1) -> window at $A0 (line39) -> yellow. This drives DB15 (p18).
;
; Mechanism (proven: db13 held o18=0, b001 held o17=0 whole boot): UA4's
; oe (=/_DRVEN) is off during reset -> UA4 releases /_CFGDxx; UA6 driving
; the DB line low then makes UA4 capture 0 at reset-release and hold it.
; Controller er_Type ($D1) intact: ROM drives the $E8 read strong, the
; series resistors decouple UA4's internal 0 from the bus the OS reads.
;
; BOARD: game II - DIP-1 ON - DIP-2 ON - JPA1 2M. SIMMs out for the
;   clean-boot check, then in to look for region 00100 ($200000).
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : UNCHANGED working latched version -----------
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) : Hi-Z (unchanged) -------------------------
ACPHASE.T = VCC
ACPHASE.E = AB1 & /AB1


; ---- DB13 (pin 20) : drive HIGH ; DB12 (pin 21) : Hi-Z --------------
; *** b001e FIX (2026-08-09) ***
; b001d left DB13 Hi-Z assuming it would float "naturally 1" so UA4 would
; capture o18=1. MEASURED IN-CIRCUIT: it does NOT -- /DB13 has no pull-up
; (net = R15.2|U17.7|U2.13|U6.17|U7.7|UA6.20; R15 is only the series R to
; UA4.18), so it captures whatever the bus last left there. When it lands
; low the base latch becomes (0,0,0) and NO UA4 /GALCLK1 term for the
; $200000 window can fire -> UA3b never clocks -> /_UA3SEL never asserts
; -> U11 pin18 (DTACK, oe=/_UA3SEL) never enables -> CPU hangs forever.
; That nondeterminism is why ATK's direct scan sometimes worked and our
; own probes always hung: same board, latch decided by stray bus data.
; FIX: drive DB13 HIGH over the SAME window DB15/DB14 use (.E = DRVEN).
; NB: ".T = VCC" does NOT give a high -- GALasm emits an EMPTY product term
; (verified via jedutil: "o20 =" -> drives LOW, same as DB15/DB14). Use the
; explicit tautology "AB1 + /AB1" to get a real always-true data term.
; giving a deterministic base latch (o16,o17,o18) = (0,0,1).
; Note (0,0,x) can never be (1,1,1), so this keeps b001's $F8 red-screen
; cure intact -- that only ever needed the 111 pattern BROKEN, not zeroed.
DB13.T = AB1 + /AB1
DB13.E = DRVEN
DB12.T = VCC
DB12.E = AB1 & /AB1

; ---- DB15 (pin 18) + DB14 (pin 19) : drive LOW while RESET asserted --
; DB15 -> o16 (UA4.16, CORRECTED), DB14 -> o17 (UA4.17).
; .T tautological-false -> data 0 -> pin LOW. .E = /RST -> reset only.
DB15.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB15.E = DRVEN
DB14.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB14.E = DRVEN


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : Hi-Z (unchanged) ----------------
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 HD build + base-latch->(0,0,1), schematic-corrected (UA4.16=DB15).

Drives DB15 (p18) and DB14 (p19) LOW during reset so UA4 captures
o16=0 and o17=0 (DB13/o18 natural 1). Base (0,0,1) arms UA4 /GALCLK1
line35 = the 2M $200000 window only; disarms $F8/$D8/$A0 terms.
Supersedes ua6_hd_b001, which drove DB12 (p21) for o16 - but UA4.16 is
DB15 (p18), a KiCad net mislabel found by continuity. /_DRVEN unchanged.

TEST (LA, roctec_ram_cfgd channel map):
  1. RAM off: HD still boots.
  2. RAM on, SIMMs out: boots CLEAN? base latch = 0,0,1? /_RAMCE /
     /_GALSTROBE only at region 00100 ($200000), nowhere spurious?
  3. RAM on, SIMMs in bank0: access at 00100 ($200000)?
